        "misconceptions_asserted": [],
        "level_fit": 4,
        "notes": "F3.4 is only partly stated: the lesson covers reduced recall in long contexts (context rot) and that tokens are billed, but never says that everything kept in context is re-sent on every call and adds time and cost as a reason a larger window does not remove the need to manage it. The demo does mention that re-sent tokens add up, but this is not tied to the larger-window point. Level fit is good: terms are defined, the lesson builds on the earlier agent-loop session and uses the makerspace project, but the Anthropic citations and the embedding-based versus just-in-time retrieval discussion are somewhat dense for a learner who has never called a model from code."
